```
$ jci-coverage upload --help
Standalone: takes a coverage file path and uploads it. Does not
require Rust or `cargo-llvm-cov` — the caller is responsible for the
file existing at the given path in a format OtterWise accepts. It must
run in CircleCI: OtterWise shows only uploads that carry a CI
identity, so without the CircleCI environment it stops and names what
is missing.

Usage: jci-coverage upload [OPTIONS] --file <PATH>

Options:
      --file <PATH>
          Path to the coverage report to upload

  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

      --repo-token <TOKEN>
          Repository token.
          
          Falls back to `OTTERWISE_TOKEN` when omitted.

      --endpoint <URL>
          Override the upload endpoint (primarily for testing)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
